<title>USA: K-tel Q1 sales off due to divestitures.</title>
<headline>K-tel Q1 sales off due to divestitures.</headline>
<dateline>PLYMOUTH, Minn. 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>K-tel International Inc said Thursday its September 30 first quarter sales decreased due to prior fiscal year restructuring and divestitures of unprofitable units.</p>
<p>Total sales fell to $15.6 million from $16.6 million.</p>
<p>The company, which markets a variety of packaged consumer entertainment and convenience products, said net sales of its flagship U.S. music operations remained strong with growth of 15 percent over the prior year first quarter.</p>
<p>K-tel reported earnings rose to $852,000 or $0.22 per share from $305,000 or $0.08 per share.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
